<resources>
    <!-- Status bar height.
         This is the ONLY status bar dimension worth overriding on Android 16.
         SystemBarUtils.getStatusBarHeight() (frameworks/base/core/java/com/
         android/internal/policy/SystemBarUtils.java:47-55) reads exactly one
         resource, status_bar_height_default, and takes
             max(cutout safe inset top, default + waterfall top).
         This panel has no cutout (config_mainBuiltInDisplayCutout is unset and
         the live device reports DisplayCutout insets 0,0,0,0), so the max() is
         inert and the default is the height, verbatim.
         status_bar_height / _portrait / _landscape still exist in
         core/res/res/values/dimens.xml:44-56 but nothing outside that file
         reads them any more, so overriding them would be noise.

         39dp is what Lenovo dimensioned for this panel. Read out of the factory
         image rather than guessed:
             aapt2 dump resources \
               work/unpacked/parts/system/framework/framework-res.apk
             -> dimen/status_bar_height_default   39dp
                dimen/status_bar_height_landscape 39dp
                dimen/status_bar_height_portrait  39dp
                dimen/status_bar_icon_size        22dp

         Without this override the build ships 28dp, from
         vendor/lineage/overlay/no-rro/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/
         dimens.xml:21 (AOSP's own default is 24dp). Both of those are phone
         values, where the camera cutout normally dominates the max() above and
         the resource is only a floor. On a cutout-free tablet the resource IS
         the height, and 28dp is visibly thin: the framework also ships
         status_bar_icon_size 22dp, so a 28dp bar leaves 3dp of total vertical
         padding around the icons. 39dp leaves 17dp. The device owner reported
         the bar as too small on the 28dp build, which is the same observation.

         Interaction with TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY (BoardConfig.mk): this is dp, so
         it tracks density. At the 360 set there it is 88px, and at the owner's
         restored 0.85 display-size step (306) it is 75px — byte for byte what
         they had on the factory ROM.

         ⚠️ Not copied from work/reference/hirero-malbec-device, which puts 52dp
         here. That is 33% above what Lenovo ships and has no derivation in that
         tree; the factory APK is the better evidence. -->
    <dimen name="status_bar_height_default">39dp</dimen>
</resources>
